stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Restart
    Restart --> AuthorityHeld: first execution read fails
    AuthorityHeld --> Verified: fair refresh succeeds
    Restart --> Verified: prepare succeeds
    Verified --> Ready: verified authority, tickets may enqueue
    Ready --> Admitted: authorized original + stable ticket committed
    Admitted --> Granted: actor grants exact queue front
    Granted --> Claimed: matching front consumes grant once
    Claimed --> Effect: no marked predecessor, private effect permit
    Claimed --> BootReceipt: previous marked row
    BootReceipt --> Effect: existing receipt commits, exact row clears
    Effect --> Terminal: owner end
    Claimed --> Terminal: authorized current execution stop
    Effect --> Terminal: authorized current execution stop
    Terminal --> Receipt: existing owner commits idempotent terminal
    Receipt --> [*]
    Admitted --> Restart: one crash, durable ticket preserved
    Granted --> Restart: volatile grant discarded
    Claimed --> Restart: unused claim discarded
    Effect --> Restart: native effect proof resolved by existing owner
    state AuthorityBoundary {
        LookupOnly --> LookupOnly: grant / stop attempts refused
        InputCaller --> InputCaller: requests admission, receives values only
        StopCaller --> StopCaller: nonforced holder intent only
    }
    note right of Granted
        Reservation ID is not a grant.
        A ticket may enqueue while an old receipt is owed.
        No grant/lease/actor/SharedData in public ports.
    end note
    note right of Receipt
        One logical receipt per eligible original.
        Retries may write the same row more than once.
        PROPERTY PortInputsSettle checks eventual settlement.
    end note
